here's what happened in the Argentina  Netherlands World Cup quarterfinal the  Dutch were able to keep Argentina's  Lionel Messi quiet for a large part of  the half until the 35th minute that's  when Messi picked up the ball in the  Midfield he dribbled past several Dutch  Defenders and slotted a no-look pass to  Defender nahuel Molina who toe poked a  pass goalkeeper Andrew snowper Argentina  went up 1-0 and went into the half with  the lead the second half began with a  confident Argentina side turning up the  pressure on the Dutch defenders in the  71st minute Argentine Defender Marcos  Acuna won a penalty against Denzel  Dumfries Messi stepped up and scored it  Argentina took the lead 2-0 10 minutes  later six foot six inch tall Dutch  substitute vote veg horse headed across  into the back of Emiliano Martinez's  goal the Dutch got one back in the 88th  minute after a hard tackle on Defender  Nathan AKA Argentine Defender landro  Paredes kicked the ball into the Dutch  bench both teams clashed on the  touchline as the referee nearly lost  control only a yellow card for Paredes  in the 101st minute the Dutch got a free  kick outside the penalty area instead of  shooting on goal substitute Towing Coupe  miners slid an unexpected pass through  to veg horse right in front of the goal  and he shot it into the back of the net  full time ended 2-2 but tensions flared  as Argentine players and coaches voiced  frustration at the referee referee Mateo  lahos issued multiple yellow cards  during the break in extra time Argentina  picked up the intensity but still none  of their shots could find the back of  the net after 120 Minutes the score  remained tied the teams headed to  penalties the first two Dutch tries were  blocked by goalkeeper Emiliano Martinez  Lionel Messi was first up for Argentina  and scored and Leandro Paredes later  found the net making it 2-0 for  Argentina next Coupe miners finally  scored one for the Dutch it was 2-1 both  teams scored their next penalties making  it 3-2 Enzo Fernandez could have won it  for Argentina but missed then Luke De  Young kept the Dutch Alive by making it  3-3 but latero Martinez scored next and  sealed the victory for Argentina  the match ended with a record-breaking  17 total yellow cards Argentina heads to  the semi-final where they'll face  Croatia on December 13th  [Applause]
 

